WEBVTT

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.500
Masuki-san!

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.670
What's gonna happen to us...?

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.880
Initial honki no jibun yuzurenakute

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.630
Shoudou yubisaki kara emotion!

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:56.290
Ano hi watashi wa shoujo demo otona demo naku

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:01.250
Majirike no nai manazashi de yume dake miteta

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:06.330
Meramera yurayurari moetagiru yoru

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:11.380
Yuuki o kamishimete tabi ni detanda

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:16.710
Initial hajimete wakiagatta mono wa

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:21.500
Furue karadajuu kara emotion

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.380
Naze ni hatenaki yozora ni mukatte

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:32.250
Nandomo onnaji kotoba o sakebitsuzukeru no ka?

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:36.130
Toki ni aimai de miushinau

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.960
Tomadoigachi na jibun demo

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:43.380
"Te ni shita mono" wa imademo koko ni

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.080
Initial no sono saki e

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.500
Hoshi no kodou kanjite

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:53.170
(Kimi wa) tsuyoku kakinarashiteiru

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:56.170
(Ima mo) kokoro furuwasete

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.040
Aishiteiru!

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.210
Thanks for cleaning up, Rokka-chan!

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:03.040
Sure.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.500
I'm off to school.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.330
Vocalists are... Like Stars...

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.830
Year-End

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.830
Sale

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:28.790
Morning!

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.170
Are you ready for the test?

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.710
Not even close. I fell asleep studying.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.210
Dec. 6th FRIDAY

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.210
Integrated Japanese

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.210
Japanese History

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:34.040
Same here...

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.830
Her sigh was even bigger than mine.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:43.830
She's been like this all morning...

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.210
A fellow ne'er-do-well
who hasn't studied for her exams!

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:49.790
Hard to focus with the prelims afterwards, isn't it?

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.250
No turning back now!

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.880
Y-yeah...

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:57.210
Once released from the trials of Integrated Japanese,

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:01.080
the Supreme Mage of Darkness
shall taste freedom!

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:05.130
So! If I had to guess, I'd say the stuff on pg. 65...

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.000
That was covered on our midterms.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.580
What?!

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.630
Don't worry! We're in the same boat!

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.250
That's definitely a reason to worry...

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:18.210
Things aren't... lookin' good.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.210
Huh?

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.420
What's up with those guys lately?

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:26.460
I mean, I knew LAYER was
worried about something...

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.880
Rokka sounded pretty upset, too.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.670
She said King got angry
and stormed out of the studio...

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:37.420
I wish there was a way to help,
but I can't come up with any ideas...

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:38.420
Well...

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:41.830
A band has to work out
their problems themselves, you know?

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:44.710
But we can be there to lend an ear where necessary.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:50.080
Our only option is to show them
Roselia's true strength.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.000
Her bike's gone...

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.710
Maybe Masuki-san went on ahead to the venue...

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:23.540
See you later, Saaya!

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:24.540
'Kay!

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.540
Rock...?

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.500
Thanks for the pastry.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.920
Are you feeling alright?

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:54.210
I'm fine!

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:59.290
Oh, I love red bean paste!

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:00.880
I'm glad.

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:05.500
I'm sorry...

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:09.500
You're always there to support and encourage me,
and I'm imposing on your kindness...

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.170
Don't be silly!

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:14.540
You've helped me and PoPiPa out
plenty of times in the past.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.540
Oh no, it was my pleasure!

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:19.960
What's wrong?

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.880
Things have gotten garbled...

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.250
"Garbled"?

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:28.920
Like, confusing and hectic.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.710
There was this argument, and then Masuki-san...

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:41.380
I had hoped RAS would turn into
an amazing band like PoPiPa someday.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.330
With bandmates who care deeply about each other...

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.710
Always having fun...

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.750
"Garbled"...

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.580
No giving up!

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.460
It's still worth a try.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.330
Ask the others what they want to do.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.040
I should ask them...?

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.000
Uh-huh!

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.540
Being a band means working together.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:06.580
The same goes for PoPiPa.
We fight sometimes, too.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:09.920
But it's 'cause everyone loves and cherishes PoPiPa.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.580
They're constantly doing stuff
with PoPiPa's best interests in mind.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.210
That's why we are the way we are!

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.500
You're right... That makes sense...

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:25.540
I... gotta go!

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:26.750
Rock?

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:28.330
Thank you very much!

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.540
Thanks again for the pastry!

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.750
Shirayuki Private Academy

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.750
Middle School & High School

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:48.790
Bonjour!

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.420
Bonjour.

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:52.420
Bonjour, Sato-san.

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:53.880
Bonjour.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.000
I sincerely appreciate the chiboust.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.880
Consider it my thanks for the dacquoise.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:05.330
It sure was tasty.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:07.960
Au revoir.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:13.250
Big Sister Masuki!

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:14.210
Big Sister Masuki!

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.210
Big Sister Masuki!

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:16.040
Huh?

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:19.420
We'd like to bring you a bouquet at today's recital!

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:21.000
We're looking forward to it!

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.420
Th-thanks.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:26.080
"Big Sister Masuki"...

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:27.580
LOCK!

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.290
What are you doing here?!

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:33.580
Please don't quit, Masuki-san!

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:36.750
We can't keep going on like this!

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:37.920
What?

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:41.500
C'mon...

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.580
Without you, none of it matters!

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:45.080
I'm sorry for invading your privacy...

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:46.130
Who do you think she is?
I'm sorry for invading your privacy...

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:47.210
Who do you think she is?
But I need to know how you feel!

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:49.130
What kind of relationship do the two of them have...?
But I need to know how you feel!

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:50.290
What kind of relationship do the two of them have...?
You're important to me!

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:50.830
You're important to me!

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:51.880
Crap...

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:54.380
And our performance today is
extremely important, too!

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:56.880
Shh! "Recital"! You mean "recital"!

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:59.750
Let's go, Masuki-san! If we hop on Death Galaxy...

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:02.420
A horse! It's the name of a horse!

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:04.670
A-au revoir.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:27.630
Rei.

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.250
Something on your mind?

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:33.500
Hana-chan...

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:36.710
BUDOKAN

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:37.880
Death Galaxy

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:40.130
Um, "Big Sister"...?

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:43.170
They're my underclassmen. We're not related.

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:44.920
O-oh...

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.710
Please reconsider quitting RAS.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:50.670
What?

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:55.250
I'm able to play my guitar like crazy
because of your drums.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:58.500
The power behind that sound
pushes me to challenge myself...

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:00.750
and also puts me at ease onstage...

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:03.130
That's a drummer's job.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:06.880
Somethin' Maya-san once told me...

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:09.710
If you care about your bandmates,
you can overcome anything.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:15.130
A long time ago, my old man said the same thing:
Steel yourself and support the other members.

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:17.460
That's the mark of a cool drummer.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:23.460
U-um...

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:27.710
I-I used to be bad at eating ramen
before it has a chance to cool off!

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:28.330
Huh?

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:30.500
Because of you, I've gotten much better at it!

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.790
Now I look forward to grabbing ramen
on the way home from practice!

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:35.710
I like your "Princess Fried Rice," too!

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:38.830
Thank you for always giving me extra ginger on top!

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.630
Y-you're welcome...

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:43.460
So please... Please don't quit RAS!

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.130
Who said anything about quitting?

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:45.960
Huh?

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:47.710
But...

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:53.170
When you stormed out of the studio
the other day, I assumed...

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.580
That was just...

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:58.080
I'm sorry. I needed to get some fresh air, y'know?

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:04.830
How am I supposed to show my face
at today's concert?!

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.380
A-all the more reason we ought to get going!

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.710
CHU2 hasn't spoken to me...

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.210
There's no need to worry!

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.040
Let's go! Please start driving!

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:31.920
You see, CHU2 asked me if I care about RAS...

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:34.290
and to be honest, I was shocked.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.880
Singing and performing...

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:40.710
I thought I'd been taking things
seriously this whole time...

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:45.130
But now, it's as though there's something missing...

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:52.420
Vocalists are like... stars.

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:54.330
Stars?

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:58.250
Here.

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:11.630
When it's dark outside and you're beginning
to think you've lost your way,

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:15.750
you can always count on the stars
to shine like a beacon in the sky.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.580
A beacon...?

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:21.040
That shining light belongs to you, Rei.

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:25.330
The path that you choose is the path RAS will take.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.540
Dammit! No luck...

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:42.210
She said there's cameras
over here and up there, right?

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:44.630
Uh... Open sesame!

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:46.210
What do you think you're doin'?

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:48.580
Huh? I thought it was worth a try...

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.040
Put your back into it!

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:50.710
Wha-?!

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:51.540
What's wrong?

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:52.790
Oh, LAYER-san!

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:54.330
This thing won't open!

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:56.580
Is the facial recognition system broken?!

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:58.580
Maybe it's 'cause you're making a scary face...

00:11:58.580 --> 00:11:59.460
What?!

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:03.000
You don't think CHU2-san
already left for the concert, do you?

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:05.290
PAREO would've let us know by now.

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:07.250
Let's try asking Yoroizuka-san.

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:08.080
Who?

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.380
The concierge.

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:11.580
Conci-urge...?

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.130
It's "concierge."

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:14.420
Excuse me!

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.290
Anyone home?

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:23.880
CHU2!

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:26.170
Is she dead?!

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:26.880
Hey!

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:27.880
CHU2?!

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:36.080
Jerky...

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:39.540
I'll go and buy some!

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:48.500
Have you been eating properly?

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:51.500
Thanks for the jerky. I'll be ready in 10 minutes.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.710
Um... What about PAREO-san?

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.880
If she doesn't show up, we'll use a backing track.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:58.500
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:02.170
She's not the type to disappear
without a trace right before a performance!

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:05.540
It's time to go.

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:24.920
I wonder what happened to PAREO-chan...

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:26.630
Think she caught a cold?

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:29.170
But wouldn't they have said something
from the get-go?

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:31.210
You've got a point...

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:35.170
That's why they're struggling against each other...

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:43.960
Wait up!

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:45.540
Hey, CHU2!

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:46.540
Masuki...!

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:57.580
Encore! Encore! Encore!

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.040
Toritoritori_kya-

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.040
At this rate, they could run away with the tournament!

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.040
Cinnamon

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.040
Disappointed there was no encore.

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.040
Were they running behind schedule?

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.040
poyo-tan

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.040
I missed PAREO-chan at the concert.

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:03.040
Still had lots of fun, though~

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:05.250
yunibaniponi

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:05.250
LAYER-san's vocals were as beautiful as ever.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:05.250
vanilla jam lover

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:05.250
King's drumming was off the charts!

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.420
Thank goodness...

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:15.210
The concert was a success.

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.210
Even without PAREO...

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:22.250
Dressing Room

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:30.420
Still no answer... She sick?

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:33.580
Try calling her.
If it's you, she's bound to pick up.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:35.710
She won't. I tried over and over.

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:36.920
Are you serious?

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:37.920
No freakin' way!

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:38.920
Try calling again!

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:39.830
I already did!

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:42.880
Listen, don't you think
something strange is going on?

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.790
What if something happened to her?

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:47.460
Where does PAREO live? What's her address?

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:48.830
Kamogawa...

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:49.670
Where?

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:50.420
Chiba!

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:52.630
Right, but WHERE in Kamogawa?

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:53.710
I don't know...

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:56.040
Start paying more attention to your bandmates!

00:14:58.580 --> 00:14:59.580
I'm leaving.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.000
Masuki-san, CHU2-san was...

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.670
Dammit! I know, I know...

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:12.960
We're outta options. Let's go, LOCK!

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:14.500
Huh? O-okay!

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:17.000
Um, where exactly...?

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:27.210
Dressing Room

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:27.210
How'd we do?

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:29.420
A lot of people are voting for us!

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:29.420
votes

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:30.380
You're right!

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:34.460
At this rate, there's a possibility of climbing our way
even higher up the leaderboard...

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:37.580
RAS isn't getting many votes...

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:40.420
They were acting weird, weren't they?

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:41.250
Yeah...

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:43.460
CHU2-chan was on the verge of tears.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.790
And she's usually so full of confidence.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:48.580
I got the feeling Masuki was distracted.

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:49.500
Yeah...

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:51.920
And Rock seemed kind of anxious...

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:55.170
Do you think they're going to be alright...?

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:05.960
You've received one new video message
from Miu Tamade.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.540
Play it now?

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:09.710
Yes.

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:13.330
Hi, Chiyu! Has it started snowing there yet?

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:16.210
Yesterday's concert was
another resounding success!

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:18.380
I received a standing ovation after my performance.

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:20.920
I took curtain call after curtain call!

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:22.830
How are you spending your birthday?

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.210
Your father and I sent a present in the mail.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:26.750
You're going to love it!

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:29.460
If there's anything else you need, feel free to ask.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:30.580
Talk to you soon!

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:36.040
You just don't get it...

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:06.670
Chiyu, Age 6

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:09.460
Chiyu, Age 8

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:18.880
Mom and Dad give me every instrument under the sun,

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:21.500
complimenting me despite my inadequate skills...

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:04.210
Doting words and empty praise mean nothing to me.

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:09.420
"If I can't play music,
I'll put together the ultimate band..."

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:13.630
"If I do everything else myself,
they HAVE to recognize my talent."

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:17.670
So then, why...?

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:34.420
CHU2! I know you're here.

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:42.880
Masuki and LOCK went to search for PAREO.

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:44.210
We should go with them.

00:18:46.420 --> 00:18:50.750
Even if they find her,
none of us are the same page anymore.

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:58.460
I've been doing some thinking...

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:03.080
Masuki and LOCK...

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:06.040
They have this intense desire to play in a band.

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:09.960
And PAREO's always looking out for the rest of us.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:12.580
I, on the other hand...

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:14.920
practically joined RAS on a whim.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.540
My voice is the only thing
I've contributed this entire time.

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:20.080
That's your job, isn't it?

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:23.830
Yes.

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:28.670
But that alone isn't enough to call someone
the frontwoman of a band.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:35.670
Thanks to you and your hard work as our producer,
I got to concentrate on singing and performing.

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:39.790
Like Kasumi-chan from PoPiPa
and Minato-san from Roselia,

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:43.500
you took on EVERYTHING
entailed by the leader of a band.

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:48.670
CHU2... I'm sorry for being selfish.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:53.750
Why do you keep talking in past tense...?

00:19:57.080 --> 00:19:59.500
I think it's time we end this.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.380
No more pretending to be an adult.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:06.330
The vocalist who only does what she's told is gone.

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:09.080
From now on, we act in the best interest of RAS.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.710
Even if that means arguing with each other!

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:14.710
So, CHU2...

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:17.080
I say this as a member of RAS:

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.960
With the way things are now, our band is finished.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:24.670
Are you happy with that?

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:27.330
No...

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:33.960
I want to protect RAS.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:38.380
I... told PAREO...

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:42.080
I told her she was useless to me on her own.

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:43.420
CHU2!

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:44.380
I know, but...!

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:47.830
This sucks!

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:49.670
We're leaving!

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:56.920
Whoa, it's huge!

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.960
Maybe we shouldn't have come here
without calling first...

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:02.130
Did you get a reply from Rei-san?

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:05.830
O-Tae-chan!

00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:09.630
Rei!

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:10.880
Sorry, let's talk later!

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.330
Under no circumstances are we
leavin' without PAREO!

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:24.380
F-funny you should mention that...

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:26.380
What?! I can't hear you!

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:29.960
How are we supposed to bring her back with us?!

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:31.000
What?!

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:32.960
We just gotta convince her, right?!

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:34.670
That's not what I meant!

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:37.210
We're riding a motorcycle!

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:38.380
What?!

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:43.420
There are three of us! We won't all fit on a bike!

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:46.460
Quit your yellin'!

00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:48.670
Which way's Kamogawa?!

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:51.710
WHAT?!

00:21:56.170 --> 00:22:08.080
Yume uchinuku shunkan ni kimi wa nani o omou no?

00:22:10.210 --> 00:22:12.380
La la la la la la...

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:14.750
La la la la la la...

00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:17.080
La la la la la la...

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:19.170
La la la...

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:23.880
Hashaginagara itsudemo oikaketeta

00:22:23.880 --> 00:22:28.330
Honoka ni hikaru yume no kakera

00:22:28.630 --> 00:22:33.290
Zenbu hiroiatsumete tsunaidemita

00:22:33.290 --> 00:22:38.580
Minna o terasu hoshi ni natta

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:43.540
Kirameku omoidetachi dakishime

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:48.420
Fumidasu kimi no senaka itooshii

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:49.080
Dakara?

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:53.790
Dare yori mo (kimi to) itsumademo (issho ni)

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:58.540
Ima kara (minna de) utau yo (sei no de)

00:22:58.540 --> 00:23:02.210
Kore ijou matenai kara?

00:23:02.210 --> 00:23:03.130
"Sei no!"

00:23:03.130 --> 00:23:08.040
Aoi sora ni Yes! BanG! Dream! (Sono yume)

00:23:08.040 --> 00:23:12.880
Kaze ni yureru yuuki no uta (Uchinuke!)

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:22.130
Yakusoku shita ano basho to kimi o tsunaida melody

00:23:35.170 --> 00:23:37.790
Next Time: PAREO No Longer Exists
